{
  "summary": "Adds a new REST endpoint at `/rest/txspendingprevout/` exposing the functionality of the `gettxspendingprevout` RPC. The endpoint accepts up to 15 outpoints in the URI path and queries the mempool and optional `txospenderindex` for transactions spending those outputs. It supports JSON output along with `mempool_only` and `return_spending_tx` query parameters.",
  "problem": "Clients relying on Bitcoin Core's unauthenticated REST interface cannot query which transactions spend given outputs, forcing them to use the JSON-RPC interface even when the node has `txospenderindex` enabled.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'This is part of https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/33808, and now that sstone’s PR https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/24539 is merged, I added `mempool_only` and `return_spending_tx` as query params.'"
